      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining the Tool**\n\nI've decided to build this tool using Python, naming the file `poll_transcription.py`. Google Cloud Speech-to-Text seems like a good fit for this project, so I'll be integrating that API. Now, I will begin working on the basic structure of the polling functionality.\n\n\n**Outlining the Structure**\n\nOkay, I've got a clearer vision now. I'm focusing on polling a Google Cloud Speech-to-Text transcription job and returning the transcript in `poll_transcription.py`. I've outlined the logic: import the necessary Google Cloud libraries, initialize a `SpeechClient`, and use the operation name to poll. I'm planning a `main` function that accepts a job ID as an argument. I need to make sure to extract and return the transcript from the operation result. I am now proceeding by thinking about the Google Cloud Speech-to-Text API for batch transcription.\n\n\n**Refining the Implementation**\n\nI'm now concretely designing the Google Cloud Speech-to-Text polling script, focusing on the `poll_transcription.py` file. I'm solidifying the necessary steps: importing the Speech library, initializing the client, and using the `longrunning_recognize` method. I'm planning to make the script accept an operation name as a command-line argument. The function's core will involve extracting and returning the transcription result. I'm using the `google-cloud-speech` library for implementation.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789820989995,
          "start": 1789820985672
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b9a4e1480014RV56D2E0McNaK",
      "message_id": "msg_0b9a4dc93001QIkfqkweHQ7xuL",
      "session_id": "ses_f465b2381ffe6Sp1kO4xlvq3G7",
      "time_created": 1789820985672,
      "time_updated": 1789820989995
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "Y0zvjDD9KcuY9Tyz",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import argparse\nimport time\n\nfrom google.cloud import speech_v1p1beta1 as speech\nfrom google.api_core.exceptions import GoogleAPIError\n\ndef poll_transcription_job(operation_name: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Polls a Google Cloud Speech-to-Text long-running operation and returns the transcript.\"\"\"\n    client = speech.SpeechClient()\n\n    print(f\"Polling transcription job: {operation_name}\")\n\n    try:\n        operation = client.get_operation(name=operation_name)\n        while not operation.done:\n            print(\"Transcription job is still in progress. Waiting...\")\n            time.sleep(10)  # Wait for 10 seconds before polling again\n            operation = client.get_operation(name=operation_name)\n\n        if operation.error:\n            raise GoogleAPIError(f\"Transcription job failed: {operation.error}\")\n\n        # The result property is only set if the operation is done and successful\n        # Accessing `results` directly if `operation.done` is True and no `operation.error`\n        # means the operation completed successfully and has a response.\n        if operation.response and operation.response.results:\n            transcript = \"\"\n            for result in operation.response.results:\n                # The first alternative is the most likely one\n                transcript += result.alternatives[0].transcript + \"\\n\"\n            return transcript.strip()\n        else:\n            return \"No transcription results found.\"\n\n    except GoogleAPIError as e:\n        print(f\"An API error occurred: {e}\")\n        return f\"Error: {e}\"\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\")\n        return f\"Error: {e}\"\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n        description=\"Polls a Google Cloud Speech-to-Text transcription job and returns the transcript.\"\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\"operation_name\", help=\"The full name of the long-running operation (e.g., projects/PROJECT_ID/locations/LOCATION/operations/OPERATION_ID)\")\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n\n    transcript_result = poll_transcription_job(args.operation_name)\n    print(\"\\n--- Transcription Result ---\")\n    print(transcript_result)\n",
            "filePath": "poll_transcription.py"
          },
